{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And dancing.</b> Dances, as in 'praise Him with timbrel and dance' (תוף ומחול)." "<b>And he cast from his hand.</b> His strength failed when he saw the calf, and he did not have the strength to carry them, so he cast them some distance from himself, so that his feet would not be hurt when they fell." "<b>And he broke them beneath the mountain.</b> Because they lacked the letter tet from the alphabet, and also because of the anger that was upon him, and Scripture added the plural form, so that he might complete with them all the letters, single and doubled."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:30.909511467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}